�  Database & Schema Setup 
CREATE OR REPLACE DATABASE LAW_FILES; 
USE DATABASE LAW_FILES; 
CREATE OR REPLACE SCHEMA DATA; 
What this does: 
 Creates a dedicated database for your legal system 
 Creates a schema (DATA) to store: 
o Tables 
o Stages 
o File formats 
This keeps your project isolated and organized. 
Create Target Table (Structured Legal Store) 
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE LEGAL_SECTIONS ( 
ID STRING, 
SECTION_NUMBER STRING, 
SECTION_TEXT STRING, 
FILENAME STRING, 
PAGE_NUMBERS VARIANT, 
EMBEDDING VECTOR(FLOAT, 768) 
); 
What this does: 
 Stores section-level legal chunks 
 VARIANT → stores JSON arrays (page_numbers) 
 VECTOR(768) → stores embedding from arctic model 
This is your vector-enabled legal index. 
Create File Format (JSON) 
CREATE OR REPLACE FILE FORMAT LEGAL_JSON_FORMAT 
TYPE = JSON; 
Why? 
Snowflake needs a format definition to read JSON files correctly. 
Create Stage (Very Important Step) 
You must create a stage before loading files. 
CREATE OR REPLACE STAGE BHARATIYA_NAGARIK_STAGE 
FILE_FORMAT = LEGAL_JSON_FORMAT; 
⬆  
Upload Files Into Stage 
From Snowsight: 
1. Go to Data → Databases 
2. Open LAW_FILES → DATA 
3. Click Stages 
4. Open BHARATIYA_NAGARIK_STAGE 
5. Upload JSON file (from your chunks folder) 
OR via SQL: 
PUT file://local_path/Bharatiya_Nagarik_Suraksha_Sanhita_2023.json 
@BHARATIYA_NAGARIK_STAGE; 
Create Raw Table (Landing Zone) 
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE LEGAL_SECTIONS_RAW ( 
RAW VARIANT 
); 
Why? 
This is: 
 Landing table 
 Audit layer 
 Allows reprocessing 
 Production-grade ETL pattern 
Load JSON Into Raw Table 
COPY INTO LEGAL_SECTIONS_RAW 
FROM @BHARATIYA_NAGARIK_STAGE 
FILE_FORMAT = LEGAL_JSON_FORMAT; 
What happens: 
 Entire JSON file loads as VARIANT 
 Each row contains JSON array 
Transform Raw → Structured Table 
INSERT INTO LEGAL_SECTIONS  
(ID, SECTION_NUMBER, SECTION_TEXT, FILENAME, PAGE_NUMBERS) 
SELECT 
VALUE:id::STRING, 
VALUE:section_number::STRING, 
VALUE:text::STRING, 
VALUE:filename::STRING, 
VALUE:page_numbers 
FROM LEGAL_SECTIONS_RAW, 
LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => RAW); 
What this does: 
 Flattens JSON array 
 Extracts each section 
 Inserts structured records 
Now your vector-ready table is populated. 
Generate Embeddings 
UPDATE LEGAL_SECTIONS 
SET EMBEDDING = SNOWFLAKE.CORTEX.EMBED_TEXT_768( 
'snowflake-arctic-embed-m-v1.5', 
SECTION_TEXT 
) 
WHERE EMBEDDING IS NULL; 
What this does: 
 Converts each section into a 768-dimension vector 
 Stores inside VECTOR column 
Now semantic search is possible. 
Repeat for Other Acts 
For each Act: 
Create new stage 
CREATE OR REPLACE STAGE IPC_STAGE 
FILE_FORMAT = LEGAL_JSON_FORMAT; 
Upload IPC JSON file into that stage 
Copy into RAW table 
COPY INTO LEGAL_SECTIONS_RAW 
FROM @IPC_STAGE 
FILE_FORMAT = LEGAL_JSON_FORMAT; 
Run same INSERT transformation 
Run embedding update again 
Since you use: 
WHERE EMBEDDING IS NULL 
It only generates vectors for new rows. 
Clean and eAicient. 
